IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  Drs  Frederick Koerner and Andrea Flieder have reviewed this case and agree with the diagnoses  Diagnosis by  Jeoffry Brennick  MD Signed On  31 MAY 95 at 21 10 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  are ten separate specimens  Labeled  left breast mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm overlying skin ellipse containing a 1 5cm central nipple  The deep resection margin is a smooth fascial plane  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan  solid  firm mass arising in the mid breast  0 6cm below the skin surface  approaching the deep resection margin in the inferior mid breast  and coming to within 2 0cm of the inferior inked resection margin  The lesion extends medially  coming to within 3 0cm of the medial resection margin  and is approximately 10 0cm from the lateral resection margin  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm multiloculated cyst is present at the superior deep portion of the mass  coming to within 0 4cm of the deep resection margin  The cyst is filled with opaque green yellow fluid  Section code  A  nipple B  deep superior cyst C  deep inferior margin D  inferior margin E F  representative tumor G  medial margin Labeled  left axillary lymphadenectomy  level 1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm  representative sections in H through M  Labeled  left axillary lymphadenectomy  level 2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing two nodules  REMOVED_DATE and 2 8cm in greatest diameter  representative section in N  Labeled  left axilla hot spot  1  count  426  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm  irregular tan yellow nodule  bisected to reveal a geographic tan white cut surface  representative section in O  Labeled  left axilla hot spot  1  count 399  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm irregular tan nodule  covered by scant fibroadipose tissue  bisected to reveal an irregular tan red cut surface  one half submitted in P  Labeled  left axilla  hot spot  1  count 164   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan soft nodule covering a fibroadipose 