compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm mass of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm that abuts the inked margin  No frozen section done  submitted entirely in A through H  with nodule in A  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  SMALL FIRM NODULE TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Katharine Treadway  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
