Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 22 CLINICAL DATA  40 year old with history of left breast cancer  now with biopsy proven bilateral breast cancer  Now undergoing a modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  TWO SEPARATE FOCI  THE LARGER REMOVED_DATE CM  THE SMALLER REMOVED_DATE CM  BOTH POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III    WITH FOCI SUSPICIOUS BUT NOT DIAGNOSTIC FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE  Note  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The two foci of invasive carcinoma are present in the two biopsy sites  The resection margins are free of carcinoma  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES WITH COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS  ASSOCIATED WITH THE LARGEST INVASIVE FOCUS  3  INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  5  BIOPSY SITES  2   6  ALL  20  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 38                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm overlying skin ellipse containing two sutured scars  each measuring 4 0cm in length  Specimen is sectioned and inked to reveal two biopsy cavities  One biopsy cavity  the most medial and inferior  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm and is markedly hemorrhagic with ill defined firm  yellow tissue surrounding the cavity  The biopsy cavity is 4 0cm from the nearest inked margin  inferior  and 3 8cm from the overlying skin ellipse  Section code  A  nearest inked margin of biopsy cavity B E representative sections of biopsy cavity The next biopsy cavity beneath the most lateral scar measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and is hemorrhagic  contains on either side of it areas of firm  white  poorly circumscribed tissue  one measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm and the other measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The white  firm tissue is 0 5cm from the nearest inked margin  inferior  and 2 5cm from the overlying skin ellipse  Section code  F  mass with nearest inked resection margin  inferior  G J representative sections of biopsy cavity and mass K L M N  representative sections of other fibrous abnormal areas The attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm axillary tail is sectioned to reveal mutliple tan to pink lymph nodes  the largest measuring 2 0cm in greatest dimension  submitted as representative sections in O U  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
