pon sectioning   there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm soft  multi nodular  tan portion of lymphoid tissue which is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  and is resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast mass  is a 7 0x5 0 x 1 9cm yellow white  previously dyed blue  ovoid portion of fibrofatty tissue  with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior black  the medial green and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan white stellate  fibrous area with yellow chalky fat necrosis  consistent with previous biopsy site  This area appears to abut the anterior and posterior margins  coming to within 0 6cm of the inferior margin  1 5cm of the lateral margin  and greater than 1 5cm of the remaining two margins  Adjacent to this stellate area there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan ovoid well circumscribed firm rubbery nodule  which comes within 0 2cm of the inferior margin  0 5cm of the posterior margin  0 6cm of the anterior margin  and greater than 1 5cm of the remaining margins  Representative sections are submitted from inferior to superior as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial sections to inferior margin  to include the nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Adjacent stellate area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue away from nodule and stellate area  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1   LEFT SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUN