Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 21 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal right mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  80   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  MICROPAPILLARY CRIBRIFORM TYPE  20   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 07 26     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm to hard mass within less than 0 1cm of surface ink  Representative sections of mass frozen as FX 1  resubmitted in A  remainder in B J  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 3 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 59 year old woman with a history of invasive lobular carcinoma  pleomorphic type who is status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy undergoing left breast lumpectomy and left axillary dissection  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION 1  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   PLEOMORPHIC TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM FOCUS 2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE 3  MILD USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA 4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE  B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA CONTENTS   DISSECTION 1  TWENTY ONE LYMPH NODES WITH NO TUMOR IDENTIFIED  0 21  2  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE WITH HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND CAVITARY FAT NECROSIS C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR MEDIAL   EXCISION 1  FOCAL RESIDUAL INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM 2  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IS GREATER THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED MARGIN OF RESECTION 3  FOCAL LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  4  FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA 5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS SEE NOTE  D  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR MEDIAL   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS E  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS F  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN DEEP   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS G  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS H  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS 2  SCLEROSING FIBROADENOMA I  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL   EXCISION 1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE 2  FOCAL FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA 3  SCLEROSING FIBROADENOMA 4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS Note  Sections of the left breast excision  part A  reveal a small focus of lobular carcinoma in situ  LCIS  measuring approximately 0 2cm  The lobules in this focus are distended by a proliferation of large pleomorphic cells exhibiting changes secondary to prior neoadjuvant therapy  These cells are enlarged with a moderate amount of dense cytoplasm and enlarged hyperchromatic  eccentrically placed nuclei  Sections of the left breast final margin inferior medial  part C   reveal a single microscopic focus of invasive lobular carcinoma  present as a small cluster of single cells in densely sclerotic stroma  The tumor cells are large with abundant cytoplasm and eccentrically placed hyperchromatic nuclei and are morphologically similar to the cells present in the focus of LCIS described for part A  The focus of invasive lobular carcinoma measures 0 2cm and is located greater than 0 2cm from the closest margin  No other focus of invasive carcinoma is present in any of the specimens submitted  Immunohistochemical stains for e cadherin performed on sections  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  show negative staining in areas of invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma and support the diagnosis  An immunohistochemical stain for cytokeratin performed on  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlights the lobular carcinoma cells  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast lumpectomy with needle localization  short stitch superior and long stitch lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm oriented fragment of breast tissue with a needle localization wire in place and a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  There is a metallic clip on the posterior aspect  located 1 5cm from the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  medial green and lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior end margins  The breast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and dense pink white fibrous stroma which extends up to all the inked margins  An obvious tumor is not identified  Submitted entirely from superior end margin through inferior end margin in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the superior end margin  cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the inferior end margin  cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the breast parenchyma at the site of metallic clip and cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the breast parenchyma surrounding the needle localization wire  Received are 8 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left axillary node dissection contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm aggregate of multiple portions of unoriented  lymph node bearing fat  which contain multiple lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in greatest dimension  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm well circumscribed  unilocular  cystic mass  with clear fluid and has adherent gray white mucoid material  which is adherent to the cyst wall  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 possible lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 possible lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph nodes  1 inked black and bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cystic nodule  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin inferior medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with a suture designating new margin  which is inked black  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin superior medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with a suture designating new margin  which is inked black  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin inferior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with a stitch designating new margin  which is inked black  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin deep   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with 2 sutures designating new margin  which is inked black  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with a suture designating new margin  which is inked black  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with 2 sutures designating new margin  which is inked black  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left breast additional lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragmented piece of breast  which is inked black  The specimen consists of tan yellow  rubbery fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 01   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 53 50PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making