Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 06 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  TWO LARGE NODULES  REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  AND SEVERAL MICROSCOPIC FOCI  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty tissue fragment oriented with sutures  The short suture indicating superior margin  long suture indicating lateral margin  and two sutures indicating medial margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned under Dr  Gadd s supervision to reveal tan white firm area in the inferior medial aspect  The specimen is received in the back bench  and an irregular white mass in the inferior medial aspect measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The mass comes to within less than 0 1cm of the anterior margin  The mass also comes to within 0 1cm of the deep margin  There is an area of firm white fibrous tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm extending to within 1 4cm of the anterior margin  Section Code  A C  representative sections of mass with anterior closest margin  D E  representative sections of mass with closest deep margin  F  representative section of fibrotic area with closest margin  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
