Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Bilateral simple mastectomy  History of bilateral DCIS  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  WITHIN AND BEYOND THE REGION OF THE PRIOR BIOPSY SITE  2  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR IRRADIATION  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm tan brown skin contains REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple  which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 4 5cm linear well healed scar present at REMOVED_DATE o clock position that lies 7 5cm from the nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white  stellate shaped fibrous area which lies beneath the linear scar on the overlying skin and abuts the posterior inked surface  The rest of the breast parenchyma is diffusely tan white  firm  rubbery parenchyma  No additional mass is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire tan white fibrous area  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inner breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue that may represent possible nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm left mastectomy specimen with a suture designating the lateral margin  The overlying tan brown skin measures REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm and contains a 3 0cm curved scar between the 12 and 3 o clock position that lies 2 5cm from the nipple  A second 4 5cm linear scar is present at 4 o clock  5 0cm from the nipple  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal two tan white  fibrous  stellate shaped scars  The first scar measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and lies in the central region approximately beneath the curved scar present between the 12 and 3 o clock position on the overlying skin  It lies 2 0cm from the overlying skin and 5 5cm from the posterior inked surface  The second scar measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and lies in the lower outer quadrant beneath the linear scar at the 4 o clock position and lies 1 5cm from the overlying skin and 6 0cm from the posterior inked surface  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows diffuse tan white fibrous tissue and small cystic spaces filled with blue fluid  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire first scar located in the central breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin closest to the first scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire second stellate scar located in the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin closest to the second scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper o