 sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 14 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lump   is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of breast  with a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  and short stitch designating the superior aspect  There is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic biopsy site which extends within 0 4cm of the posterior margin  and an adjacent REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm nodular  firm  pink mass with focal hemorrhage  biopsy site   The mass is less than 0 1cm from the anterolateral margin  and REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm from the posterosuperior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is fatty with an area of hemorrhage in the inferior region  SECTION CODE A B  Mass and posterosuperior margin  C D  Mass approaching anterolateral margin  E  Representative central sections of mass  There is a 0 4cm cystic focus adjacent to the mass where it approaches the posterosuperior margin  and is included in cassette B  Also noted in the inferoanterior aspect  is an approximately 2 0cm in greatest dimension region with prominent ducts with focal punctate yellow areas  representatives in cassette F  G is from unremarkable fatty tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary lymph nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm fragment of fatty tissue with numerous lymph nodes  of up to 1 6