rometastases   1 Method of detection  Hematoxylin and eosin  Extracapsular extension  Marked Other forms of axillary involvement  None By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast cancer   is a 14 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm excisional left breast specimen  The surgeon denotes the lateral edge of the specimen with a long stitch  and the superior edge of the specimen with a short stitch  The specimen is inked as follows  superior   green  inferior   yellow  anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm stellate yellowish to white fibrous mass with areas of punctate hemorrhage  This mass appears to abut the posterior margin  is 1 0cm from the superior margin  1 1cm from the anterior margin  and  1cm from the inferior  medial  and lateral margins  The following cassettes are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial section displaying relation of mass to posterior and superior borders   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section of the mass  in this section there will be additional relation to superior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of normal appearing breast parenchyma away from mass  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left sentinel lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm specimen of fat and lymph node  Within the specimen there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm lymph node  The lymph node is firm and cut surface has whitish discoloration in the lymph node and is likely grossly positive  The lymph node is thinly sectioned and two representative sections are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining sections of the lymph node are saved in formalin  Gross Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION , Unchecked.
