negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of breast with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm firm  gritty  tan  lobulated mass  The tumor comes less than 0 1cm from the anterior margin  1 5cm from the superior margin  1 2cm from the inferior margin  and 1 0cm from the posterior margin  The remainder of the specimen consists of white  rubbery adipose tissue  The specimen is submitted as follows  A B   tumor in relation to the anterior margin  C D   tumor  E   superior margin  F   posterior margin  G   medial margin  H   lateral margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in three parts  Labeled  additional superficial margin L breast mass  are two fragments of fatty and dense white tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm in aggregate  sectioned in cassette I  Labeled  final shaved margins L breast margin  are multiple fragments of dense white and focally fatty tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  submitted entirely in J O  Labeled  L axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm fatty fragment with multiple small unremarkable lymph nodes of up to 1 3cm  in cassettes P R  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   TUMOR LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Di