or progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Left breast and axillary contents  is a 25 x 21 x 5cm left mastectomy specimen with attached axillary contents and a 23 x 8cm ellipse of skin containing unremarkable 1cm in diameter nipple  No lesions on the skin surface are identified  The deep surface is a thin unremarkable fibrous tissue overlying adipose tissue and is inked  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm stellate firm white mass in the upper outer quadrant  5cm from the nipple and 2cm from the closest deep margin  A representative portion of the mass is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Another piece is saved for estrogen receptors  The remainder of the breast tissue is predominantly adipose tissue with thin strands of fibrous tissue  No additional suspicious lesions are seen  The attached 7 x 5 x 2cm portion of axillary tail contains unremarkable lymph nodes up to 1 3cm in size  Section Code  A D  tumor  E  closest deep margin  F G  surrounding breast tissue  H M  lymph nodes  N  nipple  Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  David Weissmann  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Lisa H  Lerner  MD                                                                             