Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 06 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE WITH EXTENSIVE CALCIFICATION  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM AND PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  WITH MULTIPLE SMALL FOCI OF INVASION  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The intraoperative diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 38                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of breast with localizing wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  yellow  ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm schirrous lesion with a pink tan nodular cut surface admixed with fat and fibrous tissue  focally abutting inked multiple inked surgical resection margins  Representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Additional tissue submitted in cassettes A through J  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  CARCINOMA  PREDOMINANTLY INTRADUCTAL AND FOCALLY INVASIVE  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
