rmined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 08 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan yellow fibrofatty lumpectomy specimen inked and sectioned to reveal diffuse fibroelastic white tissue  There are two firm nodules of white gray granular gritty tissue abutting the inked margin  Each of these nodules are a few millimeters apart measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm respectively  One section containing both nodules is frozen as FX 1  now in A  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in B F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  silicone implant right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm of thin membraned  yellow gelatinous foreign body consistent with a silicone implant  The specimen is for gross only  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  silicone implant left  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm gelatinous thin membraned  foreign body consistent with a silicon implant  The specimen is for gross diagnosis only  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional right breast tissue  is a large fragment of tan yellow focally white fibrofatty piece of tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  Also received in the same jar is a smaller tan white fibrofatty fragment measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  In addition  in the same jar there is a tan white smooth  piece of fibrous soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  The larger fragment is serially sectioned to reveal tan white firm fibrous parenchyma with focal areas of yellow lobated fat  The specimen is submitted in entirety in G K  The smaller fragment is bivalved to reveal a tan white fibrous cut surface  This small fragment as well as the serially sectioned  thin membranous piece are submitted entirely in L M  Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS PRESENT AT THE INKED MARGIN  O R  Resident  LAURENCE DE LEVAL  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  IMPLANT  RIGHT BREAST  PART C  IMPLANT  LEFT BREAST  PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL MARGIN , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Chin Lee Wu  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Omer Yilmaz  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast CA  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  A FEW ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS   3 CELLS  IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  NOTE  The isolated tumor cells are only identified on the cytokeratin 7 immunostained level  Immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 CAM REMOVED_DATE and pankeratin on two additional levels were also examined  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   1 SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   1   3 cells   Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0 Method of detection  Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE  NOTE  Results of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 CAM REMOVED_DATE  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on three levels support the above interpretation  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  SEE TABLE  2  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma is essentially negative for E cadherin  The in situ carcinoma shows areas with ductal differentiation and other areas with a lobular like growth pattern  However  it is not clear that the two processes are distinct in situ lesions  Indeed  a morphologic spectrum between the two exists  favoring that they represent a related neoplastic process  Results of E cadherin stains in the in situ component are variable  there is strong positivity in some areas with ductal differentiation  only focal and very weak positivity in other areas with ductal differentiation  and negativity in areas with a lobular like growth pattern  Given the overall morphologic features and the fact that ductal carcinomas may lose E cadherin expression  these changes may simply represent biologic variability of a fundamentally ductal type neoplasm  However  to acknowledge the lobular like pattern of spread and minimal to absent E cadherin reactivity in some areas  both the invasive carcinoma and some of the in situ carcinoma are classified as having both ductal and lobular features  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   2 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm with a 0 12cm satellite nodule  based on combined gross and microscopic measurements   GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  2 to 3  MARGIN OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  Carcinoma in situ focally extends to  0 1cm from the posterior margin  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  2  SMALL FOCI OF EARLY FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  sentinel node hot and blue left axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan lymph node  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  sentinel node hot and blue right axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm white yellow lymph node  which is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 2  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm left breast simple mastectomy specimen which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm wrinkled white nipple areolar complex  There is a 0 6cm in diameter slightly inverted nipple  The specimen is oriented with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  There is an area of blue dye at the superior aspect of the specimen  Specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated  ill defined gray white nodule which extends to within 1 5cm of the posterior margin and 0 7cm of the anterior margin  The nodule is located within the lower outer quadrant of the specimen and extends to within 3cm of the nipple  There is a focal area of hemorrhage surrounding the nodule which appears to represent prior biopsy site  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with an abundant amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue  No other discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated and lymph nodes are not grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nodule to the nearest margin and surrounding tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue  with a section through the nipple in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm right breast simple mastectomy which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm wrinkled white nipple areolar complex with a centrally located 1 2cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  The specimen is oriented with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen has been previously dyed blue at the superior aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a lobulated tan yellow fatty cut surface with an abundant amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue and a large hemorrhagic area in the subareolar region  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated  and no lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the central  hemorrhagic aspect of the specimen  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 01 32PM ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Focally  the tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 33 53PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  164  to chromosome 17 signals  147  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE