Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 34 CLINICAL DATA  Core biopsy showed DCIS and possible microinvasion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   NOTE  No definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  The margins are free of carcinoma  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  HIGH GRADE  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN SEVEN OF SEVEN LYMPH NODES  NOTE  NO DEFINITE LYMPHATIC OR BLOOD VASCULAR INVASION IS IDENTIFIED  ALTHOUGH THERE ARE RARE FOCI THAT RAISE THE POSSIBILITY OF BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  THE MARGINS ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  SKIN  UPPER LATERAL FLAP  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm unoriented piece of fibroadipose tissue containing a guide wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fatty parenchyma  Entirely submitted in cassettes A through J with the area including the thick segment of the wire in cassettes E and F  Received fresh in two separate containers  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left breast  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen  4 x 17 x 22cm  containing a REMOVED_DATE x 18cm skin ellipse which includes a 3 x 3cm slightly eccentric nipple  The deep margin of the specimen is inked black and the specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a 2 x 2 x 2 5cm firm  ill defined  tan pink area which measures 1 5cm from the closest  deep  margin  Representative section of the tumor with the closest  deep  margin is submitted in cassette K  Representative areas of the tumor in L through N  Representative unremarkable breast away from the mass are submitted in O and P  The axillary tail measures 5 x 7 x 10cm in overall dimensions  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes Q through T  Labeled  upper lateral flap  left breast  are two fragments of adipose tissue measuring 2 x 3 x 3cm in overall dimension  Sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue and submitted entirely in cassettes U through X  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  SKIN  UPPER LATERAL FLAP   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
