Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 20 CLINICAL DATA  2 5cm infiltrating ductal carcinoma on biopsy at outside hospital reviewed at MGH                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN NINE OF NINE AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH ACUTE AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  FAT NECROSIS  FOREIGN BODY REACTION  AND GRANULATION TISSUE  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 04                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  A REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm skin ellipse is present  containing sutures indicating the superior and lateral margins  A 1 0cm nipple is located inferiorly  A 2 5cm curvilinear scar is present 0 2cm from the superior margin  The posterior resection margin is relatively smooth and covered by scant skeletal muscle fibers  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail is present  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm red brown  hemorrhagic biopsy cavity with surrounding fat necrosis immediately deep to the skin scar and extending to 0 2cm from the deep resection margin  One end of the biopsy cavity contains a tan pink  firm  ill defined tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which extends to within 0 1cm of the inked deep margin  The remainder of the specimen contains largely fibrous breast parenchyma with numerous unremarkable cysts  No other suspicious foci are identified  Several lymph nodes measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm are identified within the axillary tail  The biopsy cavity  skin scar  and adjacent tissue are serially submitted from lateral to medial in A through I  a representative section of unremarkable fibrous breast parenchyma is submitted in J  the lymph nodes are submitted in K and L  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 10 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE DEEP MARGIN   SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT IN 2 OF 10 SLIDES AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE POSTERIOR MARGIN  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The DCIS is adjacent to and extends away from the invasive component  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 AUG 98 at 15 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm fatty breast with a 7 x 0 8cm skin ellipse  and orienting sutures  The triple suture represents the nipple margin  The double suture represents the deep margin and the single suture represents the superior margin  The entire specimen is inked in black  the superior border is overinked in yellow  the posterior deep portion is overinked in blue and the  nipple margin  is overinked in orange  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral posterior surface to reveal a 0 6cm tan firm area approximately 0 5cm from deep nipple margin  and a 1 0cm hemorrhagic area near the superior aspect of the specimen  SECTION CODE A B  0 6cm tan firm area  C D  Superior 1 0cm hemorrhagic area  E G  Other areas of breast parenchyma  H  Skin  I  Medial resection margin  J  Lateral resection margin  Gross Description by  JEROME T  O CONNELL JR   MD Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Staff Pathologist  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Hugh Auchincloss Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
